/-
# S2670: essential surjectivity and the stack property for the action-groupoid
fiber pseudofunctor

## Target of this file

For F := S2669D9PrestackActual.S2669FiberPF D with D : S2622TorsorData, the last
open field of the D9 reduction S2668D9ReductionActual.S2668D9IsStack_iff is
effectivity of descent: for every object S, every covering sieve R of the etale
topology and every covering proof hR, the functor

  (F.toDescentData (fun (f : R.arrows.category) => f.obj.hom))

is essentially surjective; the full target is F.IsStack (Iut.SchemeOverField.etaleTopology F).

Both statements are proved in this file (S2670EssSurj, S2670IsStack), with the
literally requested types, without sorry and without new axioms.  **The proofs are
vacuous**, and the vacuity is proved here as a standalone theorem.

## The obstruction: S2622TorsorData is an empty type

The freeness field of S2622TorsorData quantifies over *all* objects V of the
slice site Over (Spec F), in particular over the empty scheme

  V := Opposite.op (Over.mk (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.emptyTo (Spec F))).

Every two morphisms out of the initial object of Scheme agree
(AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.empty_ext), so the hom-set V.unop ⟶ D.U is a
subsingleton.  Consequently, for the (unique) M : V.unop ⟶ D.U we have
M ≫ (rho g₁).hom = M ≫ (rho g₂).hom for *all* g₁ g₂ : ZMod l.value, and freeness
forces (0 : ZMod l.value) = 1.  Since PrimeGeFive gives 5 ≤ l.value, this is
absurd.  Hence S2622TorsorData (l := l) (F := F) has no inhabitant and every
statement quantified over it -- including the ones in this file,
S2665TorsorSheafActual, S2669D9PrestackActual and S2668D9ReductionActual -- is
vacuously true.

## Why the intended D9 statement is not obtained by repairing hfree

The mathematically intended content is effectivity of descent for the action groupoid
[-, D.U]: every descent datum over a covering sieve should come from a global
section S ⟶ D.U.  This is false in general, independently of the empty-scheme
defect above.  Standard witness (recorded here, not formalized):

* D.U := coproduct over g : ZMod l.value of Spec F (the constant group scheme over F)
  with rho the regular action.  Then [-, D.U] is the presheaf of ZMod l.value-valued
  maps on SchemeOverField F; its stackification is the classifying stack of
  ZMod l.value-torsors.  For a scheme S carrying a non-trivial ZMod l.value-torsor
  P ⟶ S, the descent datum encoded by P (equivalently, the corresponding section
  of the quotient stack) is not isomorphic to any F.toDescentData M, since such an
  isomorphism would split P.  This D satisfies freeness for every *non-empty* V
  (a non-empty scheme has a field-valued point and rho is faithful), so the failure
  is not an artefact of the empty scheme.
* Concretely over F = Q and l.value = 5: take D.U = Spec K with K/Q cyclic of degree 5,
  rho the Galois action, S = Spec Q and R the sieve generated by the etale cover
  D.U ⟶ S.  A Z/5-torsor P ⟶ S with a Z/5-equivariant map P ⟶ D.U (choose P split by
  K, e.g. a cyclic degree-5 extension of Q linearly disjoint from K) gives a descent
  datum over R whose underlying torsor is non-trivial, while F.toDescentData M is only
  available for M : S ⟶ D.U, i.e. for a K-rational point of S, which does not exist.

A second, independent defect affects the prestack half of the D9 chain as soon as
hfree is weakened: for the empty object of the slice site the empty sieve is
covering (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.bot_mem_grothendieckTopology), so any sheaf on
the slice takes a subsingleton value at that object.  The value of
S2620TorsorPresheaf at the empty object is all of ZMod l.value, and the value of
F.presheafHom M N at the empty object is the automorphism group ZMod l.value of the
one-object fiber.  Hence S2620_G_torsor_isSheaf (S2665TorsorSheafActual) and
S2669FiberPresheafHom_isSheaf hold only because S2622TorsorData is empty; both would
have to be restricted to non-empty test objects (and the repaired hfree would still
not give effectivity).  Unlike the effectivity obstruction, this one is *formalised*
below and is non-vacuous: S2670TorsorPresheaf_not_isSheaf refutes the sheaf property of
the torsor section presheaf for every action-groupoid datum (not only for torsor data).

## Consequence for the D9 ledger

Do **not** record the D9 IsStack obligation as mathematically closed on the strength
of this file.  The theorems below are the literally requested statements and their
types are exactly the D9 targets; they are proved, but only vacuously.  The D9 target
has to be reformulated, the two natural options being (i) IsStack of the
*stackification* of [-, D.U] (the quotient stack), i.e. a statement about
ZMod l.value-torsors rather than about sections, or (ii) effectivity only over a site
on which the relevant H^1(-, ZMod l.value) vanishes, together with a repaired freeness
hypothesis (freeness at non-empty V only) and non-empty test objects.
-/
import tmp.sheaf.xif.paper.S2669D9PrestackActual
import tmp.sheaf.xif.paper.S2668D9ReductionActual

noncomputable section
open CategoryTheory
open LeanFormal.IUT
open scoped SpecOfNotation CategoryTheory.Bicategory
set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false
set_option linter.checkUnivs false
set_option maxHeartbeats 8000000

namespace LeanFormal.IUT.XiFPaper.S2670D9EssSurjActual

open LeanFormal.IUT.XiFPaper.S2619ActionGroupoidFiberSkeleton
open LeanFormal.IUT.XiFPaper.S2620RepresentableSheafActual
open LeanFormal.IUT.XiFPaper.S2621TorsorPresheafActual
open LeanFormal.IUT.XiFPaper.S2622TorsorSectionUniqueActual
open LeanFormal.IUT.XiFPaper.S2668D9ReductionActual
open LeanFormal.IUT.XiFPaper.S2668FiberCoherenceActual
open LeanFormal.IUT.XiFPaper.S2669D9PrestackActual

universe u
variable {l : PrimeGeFive} {F : Type u} [Field F]

/-! ## The hypothesis type is empty -/

/-- Arithmetic core of the obstruction: 0 ≠ 1 in ZMod l.value. -/
theorem S2670ZMod_zero_ne_one {l : PrimeGeFive} (h : (0 : ZMod l.value) = 1) : False := by
  have h1 := congrArg ZMod.val h
  rw [ZMod.val_zero, ZMod.val_one_eq_one_mod] at h1
  have hlt : 1 < l.value := by have := l.ge_five; omega
  rw [Nat.mod_eq_of_lt hlt] at h1
  omega

/-- **The freeness field of S2622TorsorData is unsatisfiable.**  The empty scheme is an
object of the slice site and the hom-set out of it into D.U is a subsingleton, so the
two composites M ≫ (rho g₁).hom and M ≫ (rho g₂).hom always agree, and freeness forces
0 = 1 in ZMod l.value. -/
theorem S2670TorsorData_false (D : S2622TorsorData (l := l) (F := F)) : False := by
  let V : (Iut.SchemeOverField F)ᵒᵖ :=
    Opposite.op (Over.mk (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.emptyTo (Spec(F))))
  let M : V.unop ⟶ D.toS2619ActionGroupoidData.U :=
    Over.homMk (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.emptyTo D.toS2619ActionGroupoidData.U.left)
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.empty_ext _ _)
  have h : (0 : S2619G l) = 1 :=
    D.hfree V M (g1 := 0) (g2 := 1) (by
      apply Over.OverMorphism.ext
      exact AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.empty_ext _ _)
  exact S2670ZMod_zero_ne_one h

/-- S2622TorsorData has no inhabitant. -/
theorem S2670TorsorData_isEmpty : IsEmpty (S2622TorsorData (l := l) (F := F)) :=
  ⟨fun D => S2670TorsorData_false (l := l) (F := F) D⟩

/-- Every statement quantified over S2622TorsorData is vacuous. -/
theorem S2670TorsorData_subsingleton : Subsingleton (S2622TorsorData (l := l) (F := F)) := by
  haveI := S2670TorsorData_isEmpty (l := l) (F := F)
  infer_instance

/-! ## The requested effectivity statement -/

/-- The requested effectivity statement: for every covering sieve R of the etale
topology on every object S, the descent functor of the action-groupoid fiber
pseudofunctor S2669FiberPF D is essentially surjective.  Vacuous, see the module
docstring. -/
theorem S2670EssSurj (D : S2622TorsorData (l := l) (F := F))
    {S : Iut.SchemeOverField F} (R : Sieve S)
    (hR : R ∈ Iut.SchemeOverField.etaleTopology F S) :
    ((S2669FiberPF (l := l) (F := F) D).toDescentData
      (fun (f : R.arrows.category) => f.obj.hom)).EssSurj :=
  (S2670TorsorData_false (l := l) (F := F) D).elim

/-! ## The full stack property -/

/-- **The D9 target**: the action-groupoid fiber pseudofunctor is an etale stack.
Vacuous, see the module docstring.  The prestack field is the actual theorem
S2669FiberIsPrestack (subject to the same vacuity of S2622TorsorData). -/
theorem S2670IsStack (D : S2622TorsorData (l := l) (F := F)) :
    (S2669FiberPF (l := l) (F := F) D).IsStack
      (Iut.SchemeOverField.etaleTopology F) where
  toIsPrestack := S2669FiberIsPrestack (l := l) (F := F) D
  essSurj_of_sieve := fun R hR => S2670EssSurj (l := l) (F := F) D R hR

/-- The D9 reduction S2668D9IsStack_iff with both fields supplied. -/
theorem S2670IsStack_iff (D : S2622TorsorData (l := l) (F := F)) :
    (S2669FiberPF (l := l) (F := F) D).IsStack
        (Iut.SchemeOverField.etaleTopology F) ↔
      (∀ {S : Iut.SchemeOverField F}
        (M N : (S2669FiberPF (l := l) (F := F) D).obj
          (LocallyDiscrete.mk (Opposite.op S))),
        Presheaf.IsSheaf
          ((Iut.SchemeOverField.etaleTopology F).over S)
          ((S2669FiberPF (l := l) (F := F) D).presheafHom M N)) ∧
      (∀ {S : Iut.SchemeOverField F} (R : Sieve S)
        (hR : R ∈ Iut.SchemeOverField.etaleTopology F S),
        ((S2669FiberPF (l := l) (F := F) D).toDescentData
          (fun (f : R.arrows.category) => f.obj.hom)).EssSurj) :=
  S2668D9IsStack_iff (F := F) (S2669FiberPF (l := l) (F := F) D)

/-- Target written out with the concrete pseudofunctor S2668FiberPseudofunctor and the
etale topology, as in the final shape requested by the D9 node. -/
example (D : S2622TorsorData (l := l) (F := F)) :
    (S2668FiberPseudofunctor (l := l) (F := F) D.toS2619ActionGroupoidData).IsStack
      (Iut.SchemeOverField.etaleTopology F) :=
  S2670IsStack (l := l) (F := F) D

/-- The EssSurj field written out with the concrete pseudofunctor. -/
example (D : S2622TorsorData (l := l) (F := F)) {S : Iut.SchemeOverField F} (R : Sieve S)
    (hR : R ∈ Iut.SchemeOverField.etaleTopology F S) :
    ((S2668FiberPseudofunctor (l := l) (F := F) D.toS2619ActionGroupoidData).toDescentData
      (fun (f : R.arrows.category) => f.obj.hom)).EssSurj :=
  S2670EssSurj (l := l) (F := F) D R hR

/-! ## The prestack half does not survive a repair of the hypothesis

The following refutation is *non-vacuous* (it only needs an action-groupoid datum, and
such data exist): on the slice site the empty object carries the empty covering sieve,
so any sheaf must take a subsingleton value there.  The torsor section presheaf of
S2621TorsorPresheafActual takes the value ZMod l.value there, so it is not a sheaf for
any action-groupoid datum as soon as 5 <= l.value.  Hence S2665's
S2620_G_torsor_isSheaf (and the prestack proof of S2669 which consumes it) cannot be
restored by weakening the freeness field alone; the statements have to be restricted to
non-empty test objects. -/

/-- On the empty presieve the sheaf condition is the condition that the value be a
subsingleton. -/
theorem S2670Subsingleton_of_isSheafFor_bot {C : Type*} [Category* C] {P : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ Type*}
    {X : C} (h : Presieve.IsSheafFor P (⊥ : Presieve X)) :
    Subsingleton (P.obj (Opposite.op X)) := by
  refine ⟨fun a b => ?_⟩
  have fam : Presieve.FamilyOfElements P (⊥ : Presieve X) := fun _ _ hf => hf.elim
  have hcomp : fam.Compatible := by
    intro Y₁ Y₂ Z g₁ g₂ f₁ f₂ h₁ h₂ w
    exact h₁.elim
  obtain ⟨t, ht, huniq⟩ := h fam hcomp
  rw [huniq a (fun Y f hf => hf.elim), huniq b (fun Y f hf => hf.elim)]

/-- The empty scheme, as an object of the slice site. -/
abbrev S2670EmptyScheme : Iut.SchemeOverField F :=
  Over.mk (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.emptyTo (Spec(F)))

/-- The empty object of the slice over S. -/
abbrev S2670EmptyObj (S : Iut.SchemeOverField F) : Over S :=
  Over.mk (Over.homMk (U := S2670EmptyScheme (F := F)) (V := S)
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.emptyTo S.left) (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.empty_ext _ _))

/-- The empty sieve is covering at the empty object of the slice site. -/
theorem S2670Slice_bot_mem (S : Iut.SchemeOverField F) :
    (⊥ : Sieve (S2670EmptyObj (F := F) S)) ∈
      (S2620Slice (F := F) S) (S2670EmptyObj (F := F) S) := by
  rw [S2620Slice, GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff]
  rw [Iut.SchemeOverField.etaleTopology, GrothendieckTopology.mem_over_iff]
  rw [OrderIso.map_bot, OrderIso.map_bot]
  exact AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.bot_mem_grothendieckTopology (P := @AlgebraicGeometry.Etale) ∅

/-- **The torsor section presheaf is not a sheaf on the slice site.**  Non-vacuous: it
holds for every action-groupoid datum, and action-groupoid data exist (take e.g.
D.U = Spec F with the trivial action).  This is the second, freeness-independent defect
of the D9 chain: the sheaf condition at the empty object of the slice. -/
theorem S2670TorsorPresheaf_not_isSheaf
    (D : S2619ActionGroupoidData (l := l) (F := F))
    (S : Iut.SchemeOverField F)
    (M N : S2621Hom (l := l) (F := F) D S) :
    ¬ Presheaf.IsSheaf (S2620Slice (F := F) S)
      (S2620TorsorPresheaf (l := l) (F := F) D S M N) := by
  intro hP
  let T := S2670EmptyObj (F := F) S
  have hbot := S2670Slice_bot_mem (F := F) S
  have hS : Presieve.IsSheafFor (S2620TorsorPresheaf (l := l) (F := F) D S M N)
      (⊥ : Presieve T) := by
    simpa using Presheaf.IsSheaf.isSheafFor hP (⊥ : Sieve T) hbot
  have hsub : Subsingleton
      ((S2620TorsorPresheaf (l := l) (F := F) D S M N).obj (Opposite.op T)) :=
    S2670Subsingleton_of_isSheafFor_bot hS
  have key : ∀ g : ZMod l.value,
      (T.hom ≫ M) ≫ ((D.rho g).hom) = T.hom ≫ N := by
    intro g
    apply Over.OverMorphism.ext
    exact AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.empty_ext _ _
  have h01 : (ULift.up (⟨(0 : ZMod l.value), key 0⟩ :
        { g : ZMod l.value // (T.hom ≫ M) ≫ ((D.rho g).hom) = T.hom ≫ N })) =
      (ULift.up (⟨(1 : ZMod l.value), key 1⟩ :
        { g : ZMod l.value // (T.hom ≫ M) ≫ ((D.rho g).hom) = T.hom ≫ N })) :=
    @Subsingleton.elim _ hsub _ _
  have h : (0 : ZMod l.value) = 1 := congrArg (fun z => z.down.val) h01
  exact S2670ZMod_zero_ne_one h

/-! ## The honest (non-vacuous) input, for a repaired hypothesis

The following predicate records the exact effectivity input that the current geometric
hypotheses do not supply.  It is stated for a bare action-groupoid datum, so that it
remains meaningful after S2622TorsorData is repaired; by the discussion in the module
docstring it is false in general (constant group scheme / non-trivial torsors), and any
reformulation of the D9 target has to replace it. -/

/-- The fiber pseudofunctor of a bare action-groupoid datum (no freeness needed). -/
abbrev S2670FiberPF (D : S2619ActionGroupoidData (l := l) (F := F)) :
    LocallyDiscrete (Iut.SchemeOverField F)ᵒᵖ ⥤ᵖ Cat.{0, u} :=
  S2668FiberPseudofunctor (l := l) (F := F) D

/-- Effectivity input for a bare action-groupoid datum: essential surjectivity of the
descent functor for every covering sieve of the etale topology.  This is the honest
content of the D9 effectivity field; it is *not* derivable from freeness and does not
hold for the constant group scheme with its regular action (see the module docstring). -/
def S2670EssSurjInput (D : S2619ActionGroupoidData (l := l) (F := F)) : Prop :=
  ∀ {S : Iut.SchemeOverField F} (R : Sieve S),
    R ∈ Iut.SchemeOverField.etaleTopology F S →
    ((S2670FiberPF (l := l) (F := F) D).toDescentData
      (fun (f : R.arrows.category) => f.obj.hom)).EssSurj

#print axioms S2670ZMod_zero_ne_one
#print axioms S2670TorsorData_false
#print axioms S2670TorsorData_isEmpty
#print axioms S2670TorsorData_subsingleton
#print axioms S2670EssSurj
#print axioms S2670IsStack
#print axioms S2670IsStack_iff
#print axioms S2670Subsingleton_of_isSheafFor_bot
#print axioms S2670Slice_bot_mem
#print axioms S2670TorsorPresheaf_not_isSheaf

end LeanFormal.IUT.XiFPaper.S2670D9EssSurjActual
